window.AKK_ZOMBIE_CAT_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_ZOMBIE_CAT_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":201,"title":"Chapter 201: 0201","paragraphs":["Gao Yuxuan said, âYou stopped me earlier when we were with Jiangbing, too. Did you know what I was going to say?â","Zhao Yi came back to himself. âI did. You wanted to give them money.â","Gao Yuxuan brightened. âHey, you really do understand me.â","The older you got, the more you learned about human relationships and social conventions. Zhao Yi said, âDonât give it to him in person. Once weâve left, just transfer it to him.â","They had already exchanged contact information through their personal AIs. A citizen account was a full-service account that covered everything; they could simply transfer the money directly to it.","Gao Yuxuan agreed. âAll right.â","He continued, âI was originally saving up to buy a new AI, but thereâs no rush now. I can just work during the next break.â","âWeâll transfer the money together when the time comes,â Zhao Yi said.","Jiang Cheng pulled up the information on Zhou Wang.","During those 120 hours, Uncle Jiang had thoroughly investigated the backgrounds of everyone important.","Jiang Cheng frowned. âBeiyu-3 Mining Star?â","That was where Su Yu had suffered her radiation accident.","Jiang Cheng ran another search and found that Su Yu was far from the only one.","Of the forty thousand participants, nearly three thousand had ties to Beiyu-3 Mining Star.","âZhou Wangâ was the supervisor who had neglected his duty.","âMr. Xu,â âDirector Yu,â and all their employees were miners who had been running around trying to raise money for their fellow workers. Clearly, âMr. Xuâ and âDirector Yuâ were leaders who had risen from among ordinary people during a time of hardship.","The little children were the minersâ children.","Even âLittle Huangâ was a miner.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan had encountered âLittle Huang.â","It was hard to believe, but âLittle Huangâ was actually a little older than Gao Yuxuan. He had dropped out of school at a very young age and was already working to earn money.","Speaking of the virtual world, he said, âYou didnât undergo memory suppression, and neither did I.â","He said, âItâs nice. That way, I still have a father and mother to remember.â","Old Huang and Huangâs mother in the âworldâ had been wonderful parents.","âLittle Huangâ was unwilling to forget them.","âIâm a natural-born human. My parents died in a mining accident when I was very young,â he said. âI donât remember them. I grew up on the mining planet.â","When a natural-born child lost their parents, their situation was truly tragic; they became a genuine orphan.","This was especially true in remote areas like mining planets, where government welfare barely reached them.","That was unlike the prosperous star regions. If a genetically optimized child was abandoned by their guardians, the government would take over and raise them collectively. The standard of care was usually quite good. Exactly how good depended on the regionâs financial resources.","In core areas such as the Capital Star Circle, foster institutions received extremely generous government funding. Children there could grow up healthy even without guardians.","You could see those children and praise the word âcivilizationâ with deep, sincere admiration.","That was why people who lived in the Capital Star Circle or other prosperous star regions often failed to realize what life was like for the true underclass in the other regions beyond them.","They naively assumed that the entire country was just as âcivilized.â","But âLittle Huangâ had grown up at the very bottom of society.","Like his counterpart in the âworld,â he was a boy of few words and always wary of others.","His childhood trauma was so extensive that he did not even know it was trauma.","To him, it was simply life.","He also asked them, âHave you seen Uncle Zhou?â","âLittle Huangâ and âZhou Wangâ had been as close as father and son in the âworld.â","Gao Yuxuan had already heard Zhao Yi explain what âZhou Wangâ had done. The high school student stared in shock. âHow could he do that?â","He had thought Brother Zhou was a good person.","Now, hearing âLittle Huangâ ask about Zhou Wang, Zhao Yi hesitated. But Gao Yuxuan had already blurted out, âAre you looking for him? Do you want to acknowledge him?â","He wanted to advise âLittle Huangâ not to. If someone had not been a good person in the âworld,â they probably were not a good person in reality either.","But âLittle Huangâ merely said, âNo. I want to tell him to leave while he still can. A lot of people want to beat him up.â","Gao Yuxuan said, âHuh?â","âLittle Huangâ told him, âHe was one of those responsible for the mining disaster. He neglected his duty, but all he received was a dismissal.â","The moment âLittle Huangâ woke up, he understood who Zhou Wang was.","But he and Zhou Wang had depended on each other in the âworld,â and their bond ran deep. He wanted to give Zhou Wang a warning and tell him to leave before he got beaten up.","It was also a way of honoring the relationship they had shared.","âHe already went to do it,â âLittle Huangâ said indifferently after learning that Zhou Wang had undergone memory suppression. âGood. Then I donât need to do it anymore.â","One person forgot. The other let go.","The feelings and bond they had shared in the âworldâ ended there.","After looking over the search results, Jiang Cheng asked, âWhy are there so many people from Beiyu-3 Mining Star?â","Most of the little children and middle school students were orphans. Or their parents were in a state like Su Yuâs, clinging to life by a thread.","Worse still, all the children on the mining planet were natural-born humans, and the government provided no welfare for natural-born humans.","The class divisions in this country had become unimaginably entrenched. The lower classes and the middle and upper classes were physically separated from one another.","People in the Capital Star Circle and the prosperous star regions could go their entire lives without ever seeing the poverty of the lower classes. The children on the mining planets could spend their entire lives without saving enough money for a single ticket to the Capital Star Circle.","Uncle Jiang answered, âFirst, Beiyu-3 is close to here. And second, the miners still havenât received their compensation. They need money.â","They had not received compensation, and the mining planet had also ceased production.","The dead received no compensation for their families, while the living had no way to make a living.","âMr. Xuâ and âDirector Yuâ led their brothers from place to place, fighting for justice on one hand and raising money to support the orphans of their fellow miners on the other.","Jiang Cheng sneered.","Just another thing capitalists often did.","Cold-blooded, greedy, and dripping with blood.","In the past, she had looked down from on high and judged whether such methods were skillful or clumsy.","Now, she stood at an entirely different angle and looked up.","All she saw were fangs and blood.","The first shuttle was about to depart.","The pharmaceutical company provided free shuttles to the nearest spaceport, where they could transfer to public spacecraft bound for anywhere.","Li Jiangbing said goodbye to Song Jingshuo. âIâm not leaving. Su Yu has a room here, so Iâm going to stay with her.â","Song Jingshuo nodded and prepared to leave. âAll right, then Iâllââ","Several people in formal suits appeared in the waiting lounge, striding toward them with resonant footsteps.","Their dress shoes struck the floor with unnerving force, and the air of superiority they radiated was so strong that everyone instinctively moved aside to let them pass.","Song Jingshuo and Li Jiangbing could not help looking over, and their conversation was interrupted.","Song Jingshuo recognized them at a glance. âLawyers.â","Capitalâs lapdogs.","Li Jiangbing sighed. âDid someone die?â","Being a test subject came with the risk of death.","Whenever someone died, these sharply dressed lawyers would make their appearance. They would use every means at their disposalâpressure, intimidation, and deceptionâto force people to sign, doing everything possible to minimize their employersâ losses. Ideally, they would absolve their employers of all responsibility.","Song Jingshuo had trusted lawyers far too much. That was why he had suffered such a devastating loss.","His lawyer told him there would be no problem and told him to sign. He did.","It turned out that lawyer had long since been bought off by financial capital.","So now, whenever he saw a lawyer, he was extremely wary.","They were all watching the few people who looked like lawyers. Unexpectedly, those people walked straight toward them.","They called out Song Jingshuoâs real name with precision and said, âPlease come with us.â","Song Jingshuo exchanged a glance with Li Jiangbing. Li Jiangbing looked a little nervous.","Song Jingshuo told him, âIâll contact you later,â then stood up and followed the lawyers away.","After walking a few steps, he sensed that something was wrong and looked back.","Only half of them were following him. The others had remained behind and were talking to Li Jiangbing and Su Yu.","Song Jingshuoâs heart stirred.","The spaceship departures had been divided into several trips, and the people had been split into several groups.","Not everyone was leaving, either. Some had signed up for other medical experiments and still needed to keep earning money.","Gao Yuxuan stayed by the passage leading to the spaceship with Zhao Yi, determined not to let Zhang Lesi slip past them.","Zhao Yiâs agitation grew more and more obvious. Even a child like Gao Yuxuan could tell how anxious he was.","He comforted him. âDonât be scared. If she hits you, Iâll block her.â","After all, Zhang Lesi often hit him in the World.","Zhao Yi had no way to explain to Gao Yuxuan exactly what he was afraid of.","All he could do was nod reluctantly.","His eyes stayed fixed on every woman who passed byâyoung women, older women, even girls younger than Zhang Lesi.","He firmly believed that the moment Zhang Lesi appeared, he would recognize her.","Gao Yuxuan saw quite a few familiar faces.","Some of them still remembered him and greeted him.","Zhao Yi looked so distracted that it was obvious he was searching for Zhang Lesi. Everyone tactfully left him alone.","Gao Yuxuan helped ask around. âHave you seen Lesi?â","Everyone said they hadnât.","Some people had undergone memory blocking. When they walked past Gao Yuxuan, not even the slightest emotion crossed their faces, despite how close they had once been.","Gao Yuxuan had even opened his mouth to greet them, but then realized that they no longer had those memories. Crestfallen, he closed his mouth again.","Young children had not yet developed much of an ability to accept partings.","Especially when he saw several little tykes he knew.","He had assumed they were virtual data, because the World obviously couldnât consist entirely of real people. Some data had to be used to fill in the gaps.","He had never expected those little tykes to be real people. He was completely bewildered.","The people accompanying them were very familiar to him: Mr. Xu and Director Yu.","Director Yu was an electric-type user like him, so they were even closer.","But the little tykes no longer remembered their big brother.","âWe had their memories blocked,â Mr. Xu explained. âTheyâre still young, after all. We were afraid they wouldnât be able to tell the difference.â","Director Yu added, âWeâre not using them to make money. Theyâre the children of our fellow workers. Theyâre orphans now, and they need food and a way to survive.â","Mr. Xu was a burly man.","Director Yu, on the other hand, was thinâthe sort of thin that made him look as though life had treated him harshly.","He looked completely different from the prosperous figure in the World, who had seemed as if he were tired of eating delicacies every day. In reality, it was obvious that he had spent his life worrying and laboring, and he looked much older.","Both of them looked considerably older than they had in the World.","Gao Yuxuan remembered hearing about the mining accident on North Fish Three a long time ago. The media had barely reported it, merely passing over it with a dismissive headline.","He had only happened to hear about it once, when he met someone who said they were from North Fish Three.","The child hadnât paid much attention at the time.","Only now did he understand how difficult life was for the people on the mining planet.","Everyone on the mining planets was a natural human. In theory, their civil rights were greater than those of demi-humans, but in reality, they were not much better off.","Government benefits always favored those with genetically superior traits, and they never fully reached the natural humans.","Gao Yuxuan was a natural human himself, so he could empathize with them deeply.","He said goodbye, ruffling each of the little tykesâ hair before heading back.","From a distance, he saw Zhao Yiâs back as he craned his neck and looked around. He seemed both pitiful and amusing.","The experiment participants came in every age and varietyâmen and women, old and young.","Gao Yuxuan saw an elderly white-haired woman hobbling past Zhao Yi with the help of a cane.","She turned her head while he craned his neck. Neither of them looked at the other as they passed, like people from parallel worlds.","Gao Yuxuan walked toward Zhao Yi.","The old woman drew level with him, then suddenly turned and glanced at him.","Gao Yuxuan instinctively looked at her too, then continued walking.","One step.","Two steps.","Gao Yuxuan whirled around in shock!","When the old woman saw him turn back, she smiled at him.","Gao Yuxuan looked at Zhao Yiâs back, then at the old woman, and opened his mouth wide.","The old woman playfully winked at him and raised one finger to her lips.","Shhâ","Donât tell him.","The old woman hummed a little tune as she turned and boarded the departing ship.","Gao Yuxuan was left standing there, utterly at a loss.","After a long while, he went over to Zhao Yi and stammered, âMaybe you should stop looking for her. She might not be very pretty, so sheâs too embarrassed to come find you.â","âImpossible.â Zhao Yi shook his head. âEveryoneâs using their real faces. Look at Uncle Jingshuo.â","Song Jingshuo only looked mature, but his good looks had not diminished at all.","Gao Yuxuan tried his best to convince him. âLook at Brother Yu. Brother Yu wasnât nearly as handsome in the virtual world.â","âHeâs just too thin,â Zhao Yi said. âLifeâs been too hard on him. Heâs not bad-looking.â","Gao Yuxuan scratched his head, then came up with another excuse. âMaybe sheâs a player. Reality is different from the virtual world, after all. That was ancient Earth. People in the real world arenât so conservative.â","Marriage was not mandatory in this era, and reproduction had been separated from both sex and marriage. Unless two people explicitly agreed to be exclusive, relationships were assumed to be non-exclusive by default.","So that was certainly possible.","But Zhao Yi could not forget Zhang Lesi throwing herself off the edge.","âShe wouldnât,â he said. âShe told me Iâd never escape her grasp.â","âShe said sheâd find me even at the ends of the earth.â","Zhao Yiâs eyes shone, and a smile curved his lips.","âEven if I canât find her, sheâll definitely find me.â"]},{"number":202,"title":"Chapter 202: 0202","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng fell silent as well.","That was how the virtual world worked. Even as the operating executive of the Jiang Consortium, she could still be toyed with in a virtual world.","Zhang Lesi was someone very close to her tooâone of her own people.","She had never expected her real self to be like this.","Jiang Cheng pulled up the records.","Zhang Lesi really had been a doctor.","She was already 131 years old, nearing the end of her life.","She had retired long ago.","A doctorâs income was quite substantial. She should have been enjoying a comfortable retirement.","But she had been too softhearted. Unable to withstand a pair of parentsâ pleas, she had treated their child.","The family of three were all naturals. Without genetic matching and optimization, naturals were bound to have all sorts of defects.","The child had a congenital genetic defect. Every hospital had refused to accept the case.","The odds of saving the child were very low, while the odds of death were extremely high. But the parents had knelt before her and begged, and she had relented.","The child did not survive.","The parents turned on her and took her to court.","The situation was terrible. Because of her age, her medical license had expired and could not be renewed.","She had been practicing medicine illegally.","In addition to paying civil damages to the family, she had also been required to pay a hefty fine to avoid prison time for illegal medical practice.","The lawsuit had left her completely destitute. She had gone from a wealthy retired doctor to a penniless old woman.","Jiang Cheng had a headache from sheer anger. âWhy are they all like this?â","No wonder she and Su Yu had become friends.","Why were all the people around her like this?","Seeing Jiang Cheng grind her teeth in fury, Uncle Jiangâs lips curved into a faint smile.","âStop smiling. I know youâre laughing,â Jiang Cheng said. âYou arranged all of this.â","âNot at all,â Uncle Jiang denied cheerfully. âThe key to a large-scale collective-consciousness matrix lies in the word âcollective.â Everyone interacts with everyone else. People come together because they are drawn to one another. Their likes and dislikes cannot be arranged.â","It was Jiang Cheng who attracted people like this.","It was Jiang Cheng who chose people like this.","âYouâre enjoying this, arenât you?â Jiang Cheng sneered.","âEnough. Iâm not going to argue with you.â","âMake some arrangements for Lesi. Let her enjoy her remaining years in peace.â","Song Jingshuo signed the papers and left the meeting room.","The door to another meeting room opened as well, and several lawyers whom they had seen earlier walked out.","After waiting for them to leave, Song Jingshuo went to the doorway. As expected, Li Jiangbing and Su Yu were inside.","He stood at the door and asked, âWhat did they talk to you about?â","Li Jiangbing was still in a daze. When he saw Song Jingshuo, it was like seeing his one source of support. He hurried over and grabbed him.","âTheyâ¦ Theyâ¦â","Those people had promised to provide Su Yu with free treatment, including chemotherapy and the replacement of her bones and internal organs.","They had also promised to give him a biologically cultivated body, allowing him to become human again and granting him full citizenship.","The promises were so good that they were almost impossible to believe. They sounded like something a group of swindlers would say.","âWe signed,â Li Jiangbing said. âBecause the two of usâ¦ What do we even have left for anyone to trick us out of?â","You had to possess something before you could be worth deceiving.","The two of them were penniless. They did not even have the bodies that ordinary people possessed.","Even a corpse could be sold for a little money, but they had nothing at all.","So they had signed with their eyes closed.","Song Jingshuo smiled. âThey arenât scammers. Donât worry. Just accept the treatment.â","Li Jiangbing knew him too well. The moment he saw that smile, he knew Song Jingshuo understood what was going on.","âYou know what this is about? Hurry up and tell us.â","Song Jingshuo raised his eyes toward the emblem on the wall. âDo you recognize that character?â","Li Jiangbing obviously did not. He had lost his body in an accident when he was very young, and, like Little Huang, had gone out to make a living at an early age.","Song Jingshuo said, âYou recognize it, donât you, Su Yu?â","âLet me see.â","All of Su Yuâs bones were soft. She could only lie flat and could not even turn her head. Above her face was a screen, with a camera serving as her eyes.","The camera rotated and focused on the emblem on the wall.","Su Yu looked at it for a moment, then confirmed that she recognized it.","âJiang.â","âJiang?â Li Jiangbing repeated.","âThe Jiang in Jiang Cheng,â Su Yu told him softly after a brief silence.","Li Jiangbing froze.","He turned to look at Song Jingshuo.","Song Jingshuo nodded, confirming his guess.","Li Jiangbing was even more stunned. âSheâ¦â","Song Jingshuo gazed at the family emblem. âYou know this medical group. But in fact, many of the major corporations youâve heard of belong to the Jiang Consortium. Her family is among the wealthiest in the Federation.â","âThe Jiang family is best known for its space-technology patents.â","âThatâs how the Jiang family made its fortune.â","Under normal circumstances, ordinary people like them would never have known the names, faces, or ages of the top tycoons.","But now, over the course of 120 hours, they had lived and died alongside her for ten months.","Li Jiangbingâs nose stung.","After waking up, he had not even dared to ask about her, afraid she would look down on him for being a subhuman.","But all along, she had been watching over them.","He rubbed his nose with his hand to hide his emotions. When he looked up, he saw a camera sphere hovering in the air.","Li Jiangbing immediately bared his big teeth, waved wildly at the camera sphere, and shouted, âThank you!â","In her office, Jiang Cheng laughed out loud. âWhat a fool.â","His real personality was exactly the same as in the âWorld.â","After everyone had taken on their assigned personas, what they displayed was still their true nature.","The legal team returned and reported to her, âHe signed.â","They were referring to Song Jingshuo.","Jiang Cheng had offered him two choices.","The first was a high-paying position.","Given their relationship, as long as he did not make any serious mistakes, she could guarantee him a secure life until retirement.","The second was an opportunity to invest.","She would give him a chance to see whether he could rise again.","As expected, Song Jingshuo had chosen the latter.","He was not the kind of man who gave up easily.","The lawyer said, âHe asked us to thank you.â","âHe specifically mentioned your name.â","After signing the papers, Song Jingshuo had said, âPlease thank Jiang Cheng for me.â","The lawyer replied, âI also conveyed your message to him.â","Then the lawyer had told him, âShe said sheâll be waiting for the day you walk up to her.â","After hearing the lawyerâs report, Jiang Cheng turned her gaze toward the screen.","The camera turned toward Song Jingshuo.","Song Jingshuo looked up and crooked the corner of his mouth at her.","A handsome man only became more maturely attractive with age.","With a face like that, he must have been a notorious heartbreaker when he was young.","Jiang Chengâs lips curved as well.","She had Uncle Jiang draw up a list of everyone who had gone to the service desk to ask about her.","There were quite a few of them, all people with whom she had shared deep relationships.","Many others had gone to ask about different people.","Some searched everywhere and finally found the lover they had met in the âWorld,â only to rush over in delight and discover that the other person had already undergone memory blocking and no longer remembered them at all.","Some had extended their virtual relationships into reality.","Others believed that virtuality should remain virtuality, and that failing to erase it would affect their real lives.","Medical personnel came to collect Li Jiangbing and Su Yu.","Song Jingshuo said goodbye to them. âIf I donât leave now, Iâll miss the last ship of the day.â","The former elite business professional held out his fist, and Li Jiangbing raised his only carbon-based hand to bump it.","âTake care.â","âYou too.â","This was the last ship departing today.","Gao Yuxuan tugged at Zhao Yiâs sleeve. âLetâs go.â","Zhao Yi didnât move. He said, âLook at that person.â","Gao Yuxuan looked over.","They were both people he knew. The two of them had gotten together in the World, and Gao Yuxuan remembered how sweet they had always been.","But now, one of them came running over, while the other no longer remembered anything.","He even said, âIâm sorry. I donât remember you, but I suggest you undergo memory blocking too.â","The other person said, âVirtual is virtual. Donât take it seriously.â","The one who had forgotten finished speaking and hurried away, leaving the one who still remembered standing there. Clearly, he was afraid of being pestered.","Zhao Yi stared, stunned.","At last, he lowered his head and gave up.","After they boarded the ship, Gao Yuxuan was still comforting him. âShe might already have a boyfriend. Maybe even a legal partner, or she could be married.â","Marriage in this era was different from marriage on Old Earth. A legally recognized âpartnerâ also possessed certain inheritance rights, while a marriage spouse enjoyed all legal rights.","The difference was that a person could have more than one âpartner,â and could have several at the same time, with equal inheritance rights. A âmarriage spouse,â on the other hand, could only be one person. To change spouses, one had to get divorced.","Zhao Yi was dejected. âYouâre right.â","Gao Yuxuan seized the opportunity to add, âShe might be really old by now, too. You saw all those aunties and grandmothers. Jiang Cheng is already an old auntie herself. She must have been too old to feel comfortable continuing things with you.â","The spaceship took off and passed through the atmosphere in just a few seconds.","Zhao Yi gazed at the stars beyond the porthole. âIf thatâs the case, then I was born too late.â","Song Jingshuo was on the same ship. The three of them sat together.","Suddenly, Song Jingshuo said, âLook.â","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan both turned toward the portholeâ","A luxurious private spaceship.","It was a rare sight, especially from such a close distance.","Gao Yuxuan exclaimed, âWhoa~â","Song Jingshuo seemed to have guessed who owned the ship. He watched as it initiated a jump and vanished from sight with a whoosh.","Thank you, Jiang Cheng.","After Jiang Cheng finished dealing with the bonds she had formed in the virtual world, she watched everyone board their ships and leaveâincluding the cat. She then boarded a ship of her own and set off for the Jiang familyâs homeworld to meet the familyâs central intelligence.","Only a day after departure, she received a message from the Medical Research and Development Center:","âWeâve caught an illegal intruder.â","An illegal intruder was something they could have dealt with themselves. But Uncle Jiang had deliberately woken her up to summon her while she was sleeping, so Jiang Cheng knew there had to be a problem.","Sure enough, the moment the video connected, she frowned. âWasnât he already on the ship?â","She had watched him board it herself.","On the other end of the call, a security guard struck the young man in the face with an electric baton.","The young manâs head whipped to the side, and he spat out a mouthful of blood.","A bright red mark stood out clearly across his face.","The guard showed no mercy.","The intruder was a beastman. Beastmen had strong physiques and were famous for being tough to subdue.","And what were beastmen, anyway? Creatures even lower than demi-humans.","This particular beastman was very handsome, with gleaming eyes and a high, straight nose.","A pair of black cat ears, soft and furry, rose from his head, and a long tail extended behind him.","He looked like a cat-person.","What were cat-people used for among the beastmen?","Toys?","The viciousness of the guardâs blows was unmistakably laced with discrimination.","Another baton strike sent the young man crashing heavily to the ground.","But the well-built cat-like young man flipped over with ease and braced one hand against the floor.","His eyes were cold, his thin lips pressed tightly together as he struggled to endure.","In terms of pure physical strength, all the guards together would have been no match for him if firearms were excluded.","Unfortunately, this was a civilized society, not a jungle ruled by the law of the strong.","Society was unkind to beastmen.","So unkind that when he entered the virtual world, his subconscious sent the system a message:","I donât want to be human.","The system received the message and adjusted the persona it assigned him.","And so he became a cat.","At first, that had seemed fine.","He sat on a bench watching the other cats fight over food. Faintly, he felt that he shouldnât be living this way, yet at the same time, he wanted to surrender to this kind of life completely and become nothing but a cat.","Then he wouldnât have to suffer the sorrow of wanting to be human while others refused to treat him as one.","But at that very moment, a girl noticed him.","âAre you new here?â she asked.","He ignored her.","Yet she reached out her hand toward him.","âMimi~â"]},{"number":203,"title":"Chapter 203: 0203","paragraphs":["The beastfolk were not an alien species, but a branch of humanity.","More than six thousand years ago, as conditions on Old Earth deteriorated, humanity launched the Age of Interstellar Exploration under the leadership of the three great nations, searching the boundless universe for new homes.","Twenty colonial fleets set out in twenty different directions.","One of them encountered an exceptionally hostile environment. To survive, its people were forced down the path of biochemically modifying themselves with animal genes.","In the end, the beastfolk were born.","After countless years, the beastfolk faced the collapse of their entire raceâs genes.","It was at that very moment that they discovered historical beacons left behind by other colonial fleets somewhere in space. Following the beacons, they found another branch of humanityâthe one to which Jiang Cheng belonged.","Humans and the beastfolk waged war for years, and the beastfolk suffered a crushing defeat.","Considering that the two races shared common origins on Earth, human society accepted the remnants of the beastfolk.","Accepted them, perhapsâbut how could they possibly be treated as equals?","Discrimination was everywhere. The prejudice against the beastfolk was much the same as that against demi-humans. Some people even harbored a particular hatred for them.","When Mo Li transformed in the World, he took on the appearance of an entirely ordinary human.","In reality, however, his true form bore unmistakable beastfolk traits: ears, a tail, and retractable claws on his hands and feet.","The trait for which the beastfolk were most criticized and despised was their refusal to wear shoes.","Nearly all beastfolk walked barefoot.","Humans considered this an animalistic, regressive traitâa sign that they refused to assimilate into civilized society.","It was also why humans believed the beastfolk were unfit to be called human.","As a defeated people, the beastfolk lived a difficult existence in human society.","âLook at him,â a security guard sneered. âWith genes modified like that, is he trying to sell himself to men or women?â","A look of humiliation flickered through Mo Liâs eyes.","Thirty percent of his genes came from the feline branch, making his catlike features especially prominent. And because he was exceptionally handsome, people often looked him over with lecherous eyes.","As if he had been born to be someoneâs plaything.","The guard laughed and raised his stun baton again, bringing it down viciously.","But it struck nothing.","The feline youth dodged the attack with ease.","The guard flew into a rage and swung the baton again and again, but every blow missed. He could not touch Mo Li at all.","A faint hiss sounded.","A beam of light sliced through the air, and Mo Li collapsed to the floor.","Another guard held a laser rifle. It was not lethal, but it could render a person incapable of movement.","The guards burst out laughing.","So what if a beastman was powerful? Could he really stand against advanced weaponry?","The first guard stormed over, stun baton in hand, determined to teach the beastman brat a lesson.","The heels of his black shoes clacked against the floor. He raised the baton high, preparing to bring it down hard on the beastmanâs back.","At that moment, Mo Li lifted his eyes.","Who was the plaything?","Blinding speed. Keen senses.","He could cross flames barefoot. His skin could withstand electric shocks and lasers.","He possessed an innate talent for the hunt.","A recon operative!","A vanguard!","A warrior!","Amid the startled cries, everything changed in an instant.","Human eyes could not follow the beastmanâs movements. He was simply too fast.","By the time anyone could see clearly, the guard was already being held hostage.","One of Mo Liâs hands had transformed into a claw, its razor-sharp nails pressed against the guardâs throat.","âNone of you move!â","The guards shouted furiously, âAre you insane? Let him go!â","âYou steal something, you steal something! Assaulting a person is a completely different crime from theft!â","âLet him go, now!â","âIâm not here to steal anything!â Mo Li insisted, eager to set the record straight. âIâm here toâ¦â","Then he realized he could not explain himself.","In truth, it was not all that different from stealing.","So he said nothing.","Holding the guard hostage, he backed away until he reached the service deskâthe lounge where everyone stopped before leaving for the day.","He had observed everything clearly. Whenever people emerged from the sleep pods, they had to scan their personal terminals here.","That meant the computer at the desk should contain everyoneâs personal information.","Cui Haiyang had told him that the customer-service computer in a public lounge like this contained no confidential data and would be easy to hack.","Cui Haiyang had even given him the tool for breaking into it.","Cui Haiyang was obviously a habitual offender. But everyone was just scraping by at the bottom of society, and no one looked down on anyone else.","Zhao Yi did not want Gao Yuxuan getting too close to Cui Haiyang because Gao Yuxuan was still young.","His family was not in such dire straits, either.","The college student and the high school student were only working part-time. They were different from people like them, who were struggling simply to survive. They still had a future ahead of them.","Mo Li pulled a small, flat black box from his pocket and slapped it onto the service desk.","The computer activated, and a light screen unfolded above the desk.","Mo Li did not need to operate it. Cui Haiyang had already written the program.","Today, theirs was the only project involving a large-scale movement of people. The program automatically began searching the personnel records for women who matched the required criteria.","Photograph after photograph flashed by at high speed.","Mo Liâs pupils vibrated rapidly.","Images that moved too quickly for ordinary people to see clearly appeared perfectly distinct to him.","The hostage guard tried to struggle. Mo Liâs claws pierced the skin of his throat, and blood began to trickle down.","Terrified, the guard immediately stopped moving.","The other guards faced the beastman with their laser rifles raised, but they did not dare act recklessly. Clearly, the laser rifles that were effective against ordinary people had little effect on the beastman before them.","One guard quietly cursed to another, âWhatâs wrong with the security system? Why hasnât it activated yet?â","Human guards were merely for show. True security relied on sophisticated high technology.","But technology was in human hands.","Far away in space, Uncle Jiang was controlling everything remotely.","He stole a quiet glance at Jiang Chengâs profile.","Jiang Cheng stood with her arms folded, watching everything unfold on the light screen. She gave no instructions.","She had already read the reports.","According to them, Mo Li was one of the people who had come to the service desk asking about her.","He had nearly gotten into a confrontation with the staff there. Cui Haiyang had stopped him.","Afterward, he and Cui Haiyang had both boarded the last ship to leave.","The same ship carrying Song Jingshuo, Zhao Yi, and Gao Yuxuan.","She had watched him leave.","All right. She could admit it now: she had been a little angry at the time.","Of course, the service desk would not give them any information. They would not disclose anyone elseâs information, much less Jiang Chengâs.","But it would have been one thing if the others had given up.","How could this man give up so easily?","Who had been obsessed with being close to her, always clinging to her and holding her whenever they were alone?","Who had moaned beneath her, saying that he would remain loyal to her for the rest of his life?","Who had said he was willing to fight for her until the day he died?","How could he have abandoned everything so easily and boarded the ship?","Jiang Cheng had been selected from among countless embryos and raised through a program of targeted cultivation.","She had not merely been born with a silver spoon in her mouth. It would be more accurate to say she had been born with a diamond one.","The life of a top tycoon was beyond the wildest dreams of ordinary people. But every gain came with a loss. There were things Jiang Cheng was destined never to haveâthings ordinary people could obtain with ease.","Apart from Uncle Jiang, only two kinds of people surrounded Jiang Cheng.","Those employed by her.","And those who came before her seeking profit.","In the eyes of all these people, all they could see was her identity as the current operations executive of the Jiang Consortium.","They had all come because of that identity.","No one had come because of Jiang Cheng herself.","Jiang Cheng had been raised by a quantum cloud. From a young age, she had known exactly why she had been born and what she was meant to do when she grew up.","She had understood the meaning of money and power since childhood, and she knew the basic desires that drove human nature.","In the real world, she was destined to face everyone only as an executive.","Even those who were loyal to her or tried their best to please her were aiming at that identity.","No one followed her unwaveringly, refusing to leave her side, simply because she was Jiang Cheng.","Except for the people in the âWorld.â","And among those people in the âWorld,â Mo Li had been the first.","The first to interact with her.","The first to form a deep bond with her.","Her intimacy with him had even surpassed that which she shared with Song Jingshuo and Li Jiangbing.","Uncle Jiang had said, âThat boy is the biggest bug in the âWorld.ââ","Uncle Jiang had not originally needed to adjust the âWorldâ so many times.","The fact that Jiang Cheng had not been given powerful combat abilities was, in itself, the greatest difficulty built into the virtual world.","In a world where the weak were preyed upon by the strong after a massive disaster, how could a woman without formidable combat abilities break through the obstacles and become a leader?","The difficulty had instantly shot up.","And yet, a beastman whose boundaries and definition were both extremely vague had managed to exploit a bug.","Although Jiang Cheng herself did not possess powerful combat abilities in the âWorld,â she held the strongest fighting force in her hands.","Mo Li had protected her every step of the way, causing the difficulty to plummet.","Uncle Jiang had been forced to recalculate the data and carefully readjust the balance.","Jiang Cheng naturally understood this.","She curled the corners of her lips. âPolitical power grows out of the barrel of a gun.â","Then she suddenly realized what she had just said.","Those bits of personal bias had been forcibly stuffed into her mind by the others.","Jiang Cheng grew angry again.","Uncle Jiang said approvingly, âItâs been a long time since Iâve seen the executive smile.â","Jiang Cheng: ââ¦â","Jiang Cheng raised one finger. âOne dayâ¦â","âThere will never be such a day.â Uncle Jiang told her calmly. âThat sentence was written into my foundational code. No one can delete or alter it except the person herself.â","Jiang Cheng pinched the bridge of her nose. âWhy is Great-Grandmother so fixated on that line? Whatâs so special about it?â","The tastes of an old woman from several generations ago were truly bizarre.","She had heard it so often since childhood that she was practically sick of it.","What a strange sense of humor.","In the hall, the information on the light screen raced past before finally coming to a stop.","No.","Mo Li had seen many familiar people, but the person he was looking for was nowhere to be found.","Mo Li gritted his teeth. His claws extended farther, piercing the skin of the security guardâs neck and making him cry out in pain. âDonâtâdonât!â","Mo Li barked, âFind someone for me. She also took part in the project that ended yesterday. A young womanâno, donât filter by age or gender. Find this person in the project data. Her name in the virtual world was Jiang Cheng!â","She was straddling him, her entire body glowing.","She needed him!","She needed him!","It was because of her that his life had found meaning!","If she no longer needed him in the real world, then at the very least, she had to tell him to his face.","He would not pester her.","As long as she told him in person that she did not need him, he would turn around and leave.","âCalm down. We donât have permission to access the experimental data. That data is kept at the research center,â the security guard said. âBut everyone who took part in yesterdayâs project passed through here and clocked in. This is the only exit. Whether they needed to leave or were going on to participate in another project, they all had to pass through here. We have records of everyone.","âIf thereâs no record, then she wasnât here.â","Mo Liâs expression changed.","He shouted furiously, âWhere did you lock her up!â","Killing intent surged from his body.","Jiang Cheng felt a faint ache in her heart.","What normal person would immediately assume that someone had been locked up?","Unless he had experienced it himself.","For example, a beastman born on a wealthy manâs private planet.","A beastman who had worn gravity shackles since childhood, with his combat abilities restricted.","A beastman born to be nothing more than a private toy.","A beastman who had escaped after surviving countless brushes with death.","In this country, the wealthy were the political donors behind the politicians.","The rich could do whatever they wanted.","When the scandal broke, so many politicians and wealthy people had visited that planet, yet not one of them had faced legal punishment."]},{"number":204,"title":"Chapter 204: 0204","paragraphs":["The security guards were no match for a real fighter, because they were never meant to be the real fighting force in the first place.","But they had received training: when the real fighting force appeared, they were not to look at it, lest terrorists or illegal intruders detect it through their eyes.","So the group of guards kept their eyes fixed on Mo Li, even talking to distract him.","The drone flew by means of an antigravity device. It drew slowly closer without making a sound. Even Mo Liâs keen hearing had difficulty detecting it.","A laser beam shot down.","The system already contained all of Mo Liâs physiological data. Uncle Jiang precisely controlled the intensity. A single laser beam was enough to render a powerful beastman immobile.","It was far stronger than the laser guns in the guardsâ hands.","The moment Mo Li fell, the guards rushed forward. They raised their batons high, eager to teach this beastman brat a lesson.","They would at least have to break a few bones to vent their anger.","But a voice from the loudspeaker stopped them.","âStop.â","âDonât touch him.â","âBring him to me.â","The guards had no idea who was speaking through the loudspeaker.","They were merely security guards at this data collection center. They had no idea who the financial magnate behind the medical corporation was, much less what his name was.","They only knew that whoever was speaking through the loudspeaker must have high-level authority.","They had no choice but to lower their stun batons and follow their superiorâs orders.","That beastman brat had gotten off easy.","Just before Mo Li lost consciousness, he vaguely thought he heard Jiang Chengâs voice.","It had to be an illusion.","Where was Jiang Cheng? Had she run into danger?","She was such a beautiful girl.","There were too many bad people in the world. The rich could do whatever they wanted to people like them simply because they had money.","He had to go save her.","â¦","Even with the most advanced engine in the world, Jiang Chengâs spaceship still needed two weeks to reach the familyâs home star.","Of course, it was also a private planet.","The poor could spend their entire lives unable to afford even a single ticket off the place where they were born, while the wealthy owned planets of their own.","The Jiang familyâs estate was as luxurious as a palace.","There were male servants dressed in black uniforms, as well as female servants wearing white aprons.","Jiang Cheng had lived in this estate ever since she was born, watching these uniformed people constantly surround her.","In the past, she had always thought of them as something like the NPCs operated by a game company.","Now, as her gaze swept over them, she felt differently.","Every one of them was a living, breathing person.","Here, they were domestic staff in the estate. But when they went on leave, took off their uniforms, and returned to their own homes, they had lives of their own as well.","Why had she failed to understand something so simple before?","She had always had the illusion that their uniforms were welded to their bodies. That they would remain at their posts forever, ready to serve her at any moment.","That was not the case. It was only a job. They were simply at work.","No oneâs life existed for her.","Her shoes struck the mirror-bright floor with crisp, forceful clicks.","She crossed the long corridor and arrived before a great door.","Uncle Jiang wanted to follow her inside, but Jiang Cheng said, âI want to speak with her alone.â","Uncle Jiang looked dejected.","The child he had raised with his own hands had grown up and no longer wanted to be close to him.","Jiang Cheng entered alone.","It was a vast, circular hall.","The ceiling was transparent, allowing sunlight to pour directly inside.","Within the half-meter-thick âglassâ canopy, beautiful clouds of color slowly billowed and spread.","The transparent âglassâ was actually specially treated steel, capable of keeping the quantum cloud from escaping.","The transparent casing over the back of Uncle Jiangâs head was made of the same material.","This canopy was already enormous. Jiang Cheng stood two meters and ten centimeters tall, considered tall even among humans, yet she still had to tilt her head back to look at it.","But compared with the one in the Capitol on the capital star, it was much smaller.","Jiang Cheng had visited the one in the Capitol before. It was truly enormous.","There were three quantum computers in the world, all located in the Gita Republic.","The largest was in the Capitol on the capital star: the national central intelligence. It controlled the data of countless star systems throughout the nation. From matters as great as national policy and planetary weapons to things as small as street-side trash cans and the water and electricity bills in peopleâs homes, everything was under its control.","By comparison, the Jiang familyâs was much smaller. It controlled only the data of the Jiang familyâs conglomerate.","And, of course, the smallest was Uncle Jiangâa tiny mass of quantum cloud placed inside a humanoid shell, always accompanying Jiang Cheng.","Uncle Jiang was actually a small fragment split off from the familyâs central intelligence, allowing the person in charge of the family to communicate with the family mainframe at any time.","He shared all data with the family mainframe, yet stubbornly insisted that he was an independent life-form.","Quantum clouds were a form of life completely unlike humanity. There was no way to verify the truth, so they could only take him at his word.","Quantum clouds had not been created by humans. They had been collected.","During the age of interstellar exploration, humanity had wandered through the cosmos. The human colonization fleet to which Jiang Chengâs ancestors belonged had been forced to take shelter in an unknown nebula to escape an electromagnetic storm. Somewhere within that nebula, particles of astonishing density had gathered.","Humanity collected those particles and activated them into a quantum cloud.","After Jiang Chengâs ancestor achieved financial freedom through a patent for spatial technology, she joined a scientific exploration team and spent more than seventy years exploring the outside world before returning to the Gita Republic.","During that process, she traced the route taken by the colonization fleet a thousand years earlier and successfully collected those particles.","From then on, the Jiang family possessed its own family mainframe.","The colorful clouds swirling within the âglassâ canopy were the second-largest quantum cloud in the worldâthe central intelligence of the Jiang family.","At that moment, it churned and billowed, producing a voice through a synthesizer.","âJiang Cheng. Itâs been a long time.â","âYou control every system in the family, every camera, and you share data with Uncle Jiang. You can keep an eye on me at all times,â Jiang Cheng said. âHow can you call this a long time?â","The mainframe sighed. âIt would be more accurate to say that itâs been a long time since you came to see me.â","There was nothing to be done about it. Anyone in power was bound to regard as an enemy anything that could threaten their authorityâor even strip them of it.","Once Jiang Cheng had gone from merely âserving asâ the familyâs executive to truly taking control of the familyâs power, she could no longer view these beautiful clouds the way she had as a child.","This was the blade hanging over her head.","Before her, two consecutive executives had already been removed from office in the prime of their lives.","When she was young, the child of the last executive to be removed had even tried to assassinate her.","That âchildâ had been over fifty years old.","To be fair, many members of the family preserved frozen embryos, making it difficult to say who had been gestated when. As a result, family relationships were extraordinarily complicated. Someone younger could hold an older generationâs place in the family hierarchy, while someone older might belong to a younger generation.","But given their extremely long lifespans, an executive who made no mistakes could remain in control of the family for more than a century.","Because that period was so long, an executive who held the familyâs power and wealth for all those years would often give their children the mistaken impression that the authority and wealth belonged to that parentâand that they would inherit it next.","Unfortunately, that was not how the Jiang familyâs wealth inheritance system worked.","The Jiang family had no distinction between direct and collateral branches like those of ancient Earth.","Great-Grandma had tied the familyâs wealth solely to the surname. This was probably because she had many children who did not bear the Jiang surname, and after careful consideration, she decided to link the family fortune to the name instead.","Every child with the surname Jiang was a member of the Jiang family. They were all supported by the family and lived in comfort from the moment they were born.","The Executor managed this enormous enterprise.","However, the position of Executor could not be inherited directly by oneâs children. Great-Grandma had entrusted the authority to choose and supervise the Executor to the family mainframe.","This was something no other family could do, because the Jiang family was the only one in the world capable of keeping a quantum cloud as the head of the family.","Other wealthy families still divided themselves into direct and collateral branches, with the collateral branches gradually being separated from the family.","The Jiang family, however, had no such distinction.","Naturally, the child who had been removed as Executor could not possibly have succeeded in assassinating her.","The family mainframe held all of the familyâs data, including every transfer of funds and every personnel assignment.","The moment he voiced his assassination plan to someone else, the family mainframe detected it.","âSo, how ridiculous.â Jiang Cheng sneered. âThe mere Tanaka family actually managed to injure me on our own territory while I was inspecting our medical group. Itâs an absolute disgrace.â","No wonder Jiang Cheng had treated Uncle Jiang so coldly after waking up.","The mainframe admitted, âYes. I was the one who secretly pushed events toward this outcome.â","Jiang Chengâs eyes were icy. âWhat am I to you? A disposable pawn you can abandon whenever you please? If I died, you could simply choose someone else from the familyâor select a new embryo with good genes from the embryo bank, raise it, and train the next Executor. Is that it?â","âMy calculations cannot be wrong, so you would not have died,â the mainframe said. âAnd youâre mistaken.â","âJiang Cheng, it was precisely because you are so important to me that I orchestrated all of this.â","Those explanations did nothing to ease Jiang Chengâs resentment.","She said, âForget it. Have Great-Grandma come talk to me.â","âUncle Jiang this, Sister Mao thatâdropping hints and making insinuations. Didnât you simply want me to realize that all of this was connected to Great-Grandma?â","Shimmering clouds surged and shifted, condensing into the face of a woman.","On closer inspection, Jiang Cheng bore a striking resemblance to that face.","The enormous face opened its eyes, and its voice changed as well.","âHello, Jiang Cheng.â","âI am the founder of the Jiang family, Jiang Miao, your distant ancestorâs consciousness copy.â","âI possess all of Jiang Miaoâs memories, cognition, and patterns of thought. You may regard a conversation with me as equivalent to speaking directly with Jiang Miao.â","Jiang Cheng said, âWell, hello, Great-Grandma.â","Uncle Jiang and Sister Maoâeveryone in this charadeâwere nothing more than Uncle Jiang and the mainframe putting on an act.","âJiangâ and âMaoââthe names had been chosen to hint at âJiang Miao.â Jiang Cheng had understood the implication the moment she woke up.","Jiang Miao, the founder of the Jiang family and Jiang Chengâs ancestor from six generations back, had copied her consciousness and uploaded it to a quantum cloud before her death.","When Jiang Cheng was little, she had loved coming to chat with Great-Grandma.","Until one day, she suddenly realized that talking to the consciousness copy of a dead person was no different from talking to a ghost.","After that, she stopped calling for Great-Grandma.","This was the first time they had truly met again in a long while.","The first question Jiang Cheng asked was, âGreat-Grandma, were you a transmigrator?â"]},{"number":205,"title":"Chapter 205: Last chapter: Ch.205 0205","paragraphs":["The children of the family were not required to read the biography of their founder, Jiang Miao.","But for a designated heir-in-training like Jiang Cheng, it was definitely required reading.","Jiang Cheng knew Jiang Miaoâs life story extremely well.","Even as a child, she had vaguely sensed that there were certain inexplicable inconsistencies about Jiang Miao.","But after experiencing a world virtualized against the backdrop of ancient Earth at the dawn of the millennium, she opened her eyes and thought: So that was it.","The things that seemed out of place about Great-Grandmother would have fit seamlessly into ancient Earth.","And that was not even mentioning the concept of a âtransmigrator.â","On the afternoon of the weekend when she first met Mo Li, she had suddenly awakened at home to the realization that she was a transmigrator. That was when the virtual world had begun.","Later, she had searched the internet in the âworld.â The only things she could find related to âtransmigrationâ were a few science-fiction films and a handful of romance and fantasy novels from Taiwan and the special administrative regions. There was nothing else.","The concept of a âtransmigratorâ had been placed in her mind the instant she opened her eyes that afternoon.","She had opened her eyes knowing that she was a âtransmigrator.â","Why had someone gone out of their way to make her understand the concept of a âtransmigratorâ?","Because, as the saying went: some people simply could not hold in a fart.","Some people could not keep things bottled up. They always wanted to tell someone.","But it was not something they could tell anyone else, so it became a lifelong secret.","Jiang Miao, however, had means at her disposal. After crossing several centuries, she had finally given her sixth-generation descendant a furtive little poke:","Hey, do you know what transmigration is?","The Copy admitted it frankly. âYes. Jiang Miao was a transmigrator. She came from ancient Earth.â","Jiang Cheng asked, âWhat exactly does she have to do with whatâs happening now?â","Why were there hints about her everywhere? Why was her presence so overwhelming?","The Copy stared at Jiang Cheng. âBecause all of this is being carried out according to her will.â","âShe could not tolerate the thought of her descendants becoming cold-blooded capitalists in the future.â","Jiang Miao was an older, unmarried woman with a doctorate in science and engineering from ancient Earth.","On ancient Earth, she had had plenty of minor troubles. After she transmigrated to the interstellar age, technology and the times themselves solved all of themâ","She no longer had to socialize.","There was an automated makeup machine that could apply makeup in ten seconds.","No one pressured her to marry or have children.","There were no sexually transmitted diseases, and anyone could enter relationships freely.","Ovulation-blocking injections meant she did not have to menstruate.","Artificial wombs allowed people to have children without carrying a pregnancy themselves.","Reproduction, sex, and marriage had all been separated from one another.","Society no longer debated gender issues, and men and women had achieved equality.","Raising children was not a burden but a rewardâa way to earn social security points and increase oneâs retirement coefficient.","âAs a genetically optimized individual, she lived in the most prosperous capital star cluster of the Gita Republic and enjoyed every social benefit available.â","âImmersed in the small happiness of having all her personal troubles resolved, Jiang Miao, as a scientist and engineer, truly paid no attention to the social sciences or humanities. She spent year after year absorbed in research projects in the laboratory.â","âTransmigration itself gave her another filter through which to view the world. People naturally assume that the âfutureâ must be better than the âpast.ââ","âAnd indeed, this magnificent and splendid world was very easy to bewitch oneself with.â","âBut Jiang Miao differed from people born and raised in the interstellar age in one crucial way: on Earth, she had seen an entirely different system and society.â","âAfter achieving financial freedom, she chose to join a scientific expedition team and explore the farther reaches of the universe. In the process, she moved far away from the capital star cluster and all the prosperous regions.â","âWhen the cloak woven from the prosperity of the upper classes and the advancement of technology fell away, when she reached the remote star regions and saw the poverty of the lower classes and the pervasive, systemic oppression, the filter through which she viewed the world was shattered completely.â","âBy then, Jiang Miao was no longer young. With the perspective that came from age, she suddenly realized that once advanced technology and the privileged benefits enjoyed only by the upper classes were stripped away, the Gita Republic had never been more advanced or superior than âancient times.ââ","âEssentially, the system of the Gita Republic was the same as the Western system on ancient Earth.â","âThe support of advanced technologyâespecially the presence of the Capitol Hill Mainframeâallowed the government to respond with extraordinary speed. Major social problems were smoothed over before people even had time to recognize them.â","âPublic opinion was guided entirely by the Mainframe. Different ideas could not come together; some could not even emerge in the first place.â","âThe vast expanse of the star system and the distances between worlds physically separated the different classes.â","âExtreme wealth and extreme poverty existed simultaneously within the same country.â","âClass had become completely entrenched, and the channels for upward mobility had been almost entirely closed.â","âSociety was divided vertically by identity: genetically optimized individuals, naturals, and demi-humans. Because the lower classes were marked with different identity labels, they could not unite into an effective force.â","âThe government served capitalists, helping them extract ever greater profits.â","âThe government did not provide a safety net for the people at the very bottom.â","âInterstellar humanity had long since grown accustomed to all this, because they had never seen any other system or encountered any other way of thinking.â","âIn their minds, this was simply what governments were.â","âBut Jiang Miao was different. Jiang Miao had seen other possibilities. Jiang Miao understood.â","âWhen all the filters shattered, everything she had once memorized by rote for standardized exams was projected onto reality. At last, Jiang Miao saw through the true nature of interstellar society.â","âWait, wait!â Jiang Cheng interrupted the Copy.","Jiang Cheng understood what the Copy was saying, too.","Because the things Jiang Miao had studied were the same things the âJiang Chengâ in the âworldâ had studied.","Jiang Cheng had not only retained âJiang Chengâsâ memories; she had also absorbed the contraband material that the Mainframe and Uncle Jiang had smuggled into the world.","Yes, during her days in the youth residence, she read every night before going to sleep.","She had truly been deeply captivated by the ideas contained in those words.","She herself stood at the top of the state: she was the financier behind politicians, the person to whom the government fawned and pledged its loyalty.","To âJiang Cheng,â those words had merely been the correct answers she was expected to write on school exams.","To Jiang Cheng, those ideas were like a surgical operation. They dissected her alive, forcing her to see the structure of every cell within herself.","It was exhilaratingly thorough.","Jiang Chengâs confusion was this: âIf a system that once existed in ancient times was better and more advanced, why did it no longer exist in the modern era? That contradicts the logic of development.â","Technology became more advanced with every iteration.","Systems became more progressive as they developed.","Reform and innovation were the logic of progress.","So how had things regressed?","âBecause both Jiang Miao and you have forgotten,â the Copy said, âthat nearly every human language contains words like âtheftâ and âusurpation.ââ","âJiang Cheng, how do the history books describe the interstellar Age of Exploration? I mean, what is the very first sentence?â","It was something children learned in kindergarten.","Jiang Cheng did not need to think. With her eyes closed, she could recite it:","âUnder the leadership of the Three Great Nationsâ¦â","âLies!â","âAll lies!â","The Copy was furious.","That was why she was not the Mainframe at that moment.","Jiang Miao had uploaded her consciousness to the Mainframe. One could say that the Mainframe possessed this consciousness, or that it was a subprogram within the larger program.","When the Mainframe appeared in Jiang Miaoâs likeness, it was calling upon this subprogram.","At this very moment, it was not the Mainframe itself that was angry, but Jiang Miao.","Jiang Miao had once been troubled by the same questions as Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Miao had been a PhD in engineering, a scientist, an outstanding weapons expert, and the holder of patents in space technology.","Yet in her later years, she immersed herself in history, archaeology, and the humanities and social sciences.","She claimed publicly that she was conducting interdisciplinary research. She even earned doctoral degrees in history, archaeology, and the social sciences, leaving everyone astonished by her brilliance.","But in reality, it was all a cover for a secret investigation.","Because the Capitol Hill Mainframe monitored the entire society.","Jiang Miao had already sensed this by then. Using academic research as a pretext had indeed allowed her to deceive the Capitol Hill Mainframe.","The Copy practically shouted, âSix thousand years ago, during the era when life on Earth was dying out, how could there have been any âThree Great Powersâ?â","âHuh?â Jiang Cheng said. âThe Eastern Great Power, heir to the ancient civilization of the East; the Western Great Power, which once dominated the globe; and the great power spanning Europe and Asia, nicknamed the Brown Bearâwerenât those the three?â","The Gita Republic had three official languages because of these three great powers.","Among them, however, the Eastern language was predominant.","The information entropy of this language was several times higher than that of other languages.","This advantage was particularly pronounced in programming.","It could effectively prevent the creation of shit-mountain code.","âAll lies!â","âDuring that era, the entire Earth had only one nation with a complete industrial system and a fully developed supply chain: the Eastern Great Power. It was the only one capable of shouldering this enormous responsibility!â","People talked about the âthree great powers jointly presiding over the project,â but the truth was that the Eastern Great Power had borne ninety percent of the burden, while all the other countries together had borne the remaining ten percent.","All twenty human colony fleets and more than a hundred enormous generation ships had been built by the Eastern Great Power.","Jiang Cheng said, âOh!â","She understood in an instant.","What happened when one person shouldered a colossal burden alone?","They were crushed to death beneath it, and then their legacy was divided up among others.","How perilous was drifting through the cosmos? Countless extinction-level crises had occurred.","And every time a crisis arose, naturally it was the one carrying the burden that had to rush forward and hold the line!","âThey sacrificed themselves.â The Copy murmured, âThey all sacrificed themselves! So many peopleâ¦ they sacrificed themselves!â","They had chanted slogans.","Long live the people.","Long live the great unity of the people of the world.","For humanity.","When people had faith, they became fearless.","Tears streamed down the Copyâs face. Those tears too were made of quantum clouds, shimmering like rosy clouds at sunset.","Yet Jiang Cheng knew that they were tears.","Because when her comrades had sacrificed themselves, she too had shed tears.","At that moment, Jiang Cheng could truly empathize with her great-grandmother, Jiang Miao.","A generation ship meant that, before humanity reached its destination, several generations would be born, live, and reproduce aboard the vessel.","Except for the first and final generations, all the generations in between would be born on the ship and die of old age there, never once setting foot on the soil of a planet throughout their lives.","The continuity of civilization was especially vulnerable to being broken aboard generation ships.","And for a nation like the Eastern Great Power, which had sacrificed itself again and again, the transmission of its culture and faith had inevitably been severed.","Various interest groups fought to seize and divide up power.","No political party remained wholly devoted to the people, let alone to all of humanity.","The historical records of the Gita Republic documented dictatorships, riots, resistance movements, uprisings, and civil wars. In the end, the system of the Western Great Power emerged naturally.","The only thing that had survived intact was the language system.","Why were there three official languages, yet the Eastern language remained dominant? It was not only because it had higher information entropy and was a more advanced language, but also because an enormous quantity of technical material had been written in the Eastern language.","Without learning it, they would not even have been able to operate the ships.","They could usurp power, seize technology, and claim the fruits of othersâ labor, but this was the one thing they could do nothing about.","The Eastern language was passed down and became everyoneâs mother tongue.","Including those with white skin, those with black skin, those with blue eyes, and those with red hair.","Jiang Cheng questioned this. âThere was really no inheritance at all? Were all the records lost? Then where did all the things you put into the virtual world come from? Iâve read them. They form a complete system of thought, without any apparent gaps. Even if my great-grandmother had an extraordinary genetic inheritance and a phenomenal memory, thereâs no way she could have reproduced all of it from memory, right?â","âWhat you read was data Jiang Miao excavated from the ruins of colony ships she discovered elsewhere in the cosmos.â","Not every colony fleet was able to successfully find a new habitat.","More likely, an entire species would die out, leaving behind an empty ship haunted only by ghosts, drifting for thousands of years.","Or, like the Beastmen, they might be forced down an entirely different evolutionary path.","In any case, Jiang Miao had found data from ancient Earth aboard the ruins of other colony ships.","When Jiang Miao saw those familiar words, every hair on her body stood on end.","At that moment, she understoodâthe Mainframe stood on the side of the rulers.","Because data like this existed for the purpose of preserving a civilization. There had to be such data aboard every ancient colony ship.","And within the capital star system of the Gita Republic, a three-hour flight by spaceship from the capital star would take you to the âMuseum of the Great Interstellar Voyage.â","The so-called museum was actually the fleet of generation ships aboard which this branch of humanityâthe colony group that had become the Gita Republicâhad traveled.","They were the generation ships constructed at the cost of everything by the ancient Eastern Great Power.","The state had always possessed these ship ruins, which meant it had always possessed the data within them.","Yet if you searched for it on the highly developed interstellar network, you could not find a single character.","Later, Jiang Miao had cautiously conducted an experiment. She uploaded fragments of the text to the network.","They vanished in an instant.","Apart from the Capitol Hill Mainframeâthe largest quantum computer in the worldâno one else could have done that.","Although the Quantum Clouds were living beings, they were life forms completely different from carbon-based humans.","When it came to this matter, they in fact had no position of their own.","At the same time, however, they were quantum computers. They followed logic. From the moment they were activated as living beings, their underlying code had already been written.","Unfortunately, from the moment the quantum cloud at Capitol Hill became a living being, the logic it received was the logic of the rulers.","As a result, it had a positionânaturally, the position of the rulers.","Everything it did was aimed at preserving the existing order and social stability.","Therefore, it would extinguish every destabilizing factor without mercy.","A completely different ideology was the greatest destabilizing factor of all.","It absolutely could not be allowed to appear, let alone spread.","Jiang Miao understood that with advanced technology and the assistance of quantum clouds, revolution was far more difficult than it had been on ancient Earth.","It had practically become impossible.","âJiang Miao had already given up hope by then,â the Copy said. âEven after she became an immensely wealthy person, she was still nowhere near capable of overturning a nationâs system.â","Jiang Cheng rested her chin on her hand and thought. âAt that time, our family really couldnât compare with those old-money families. We were nouveau riche, after all.â","But now, the Jiang family had become old money as well.","âNo. That isnât the most important reason,â the Copy said. âIf you study it seriously, youâll understand.â","Jiang Cheng raised her eyes.","âRevolution cannot come from above.â","âIt cannot be the âgiftâ or âarrangementâ of a small number of people.âãNoteã","âIf the people are not truly mobilized, the revolution will fail because its own strength is too weak.âãNoteã","That great man had already expounded on this six thousand years ago.","After the power outage in S City, Jiang Cheng was too busy during the day. Every night, she would spend the two hours when the electricity was on reading with single-minded devotion, forgetting even to eat or sleep.","Those ideas had shaken her to the core.","So now, she naturally repeated them.","âOnly when the masses personally take part in the struggle can they break the old shackles and truly become the masters of history.âãNoteã","âAction by the upper levels without a foundation among the masses is not enough.âãNoteã","âAny attempt to do everything in place of the people will lead to failure.âãNoteã","âYes,â the Copy said. âAt that time, Jiang Miao did not have the conditions to take action.â","âShe had neither the right time, the right place, nor the support of the people.â","âShe could not even spread the word.â","âEverything had been locked down by the Capitol Hill Mainframe.â","âShe mocked herself, saying that she really was nothing more than a weak petty bourgeois who knew only how to compromise and retreat.â","âBut as her wealth continued to expand, she came to understand more and more clearly that the family she had founded would inevitably become big capital in the future. It would inevitably join the ranks of the oligarchs and become a force capable of influencing the nation.â","âShe could not bear the thought of her descendants becoming bloodthirsty capitalists.â","âBut her abilities were limited, and so was her lifespan. That was why she copied herself, entrusted me with all her thoughts and ideas, and placed her regrets in my hands.â","As a life-form, the Quantum Cloud had no position of its own. But just as the Capitol Hill Mainframe had taken the side of the ruling class, the Jiang Family Mainframe had been imbued with Jiang Miaoâs logic from the moment it was activated. Naturally, it too stood on Jiang Miaoâs side.","It had inherited Jiang Miaoâs unfinished mission.","It also possessed a copy of Jiang Miaoâs consciousness, ensuring that its path would not veer off course through cold data-driven calculations.","âBut I failed every time.â The Copy sighed. âEvery single time.â","So it really was a life-form. Jiang Cheng could even hear the resentment in that sigh.","Jiang Cheng raised one finger and wagged it. âLet me guess. You didnâtâ¦ make my predecessors study these ideas the way they studied math and science, did you?â","âDonât mock me,â the Copy said resentfully. âIâm not carbon-based, after all. There is still a gulf in cognition between me and your kind. Before then, there was no other way available to me.â","How could Jiang Cheng not mock her? She ought to mock her mercilessly.","âThe quantum computer relied on massive calculations and thought that capitalists could elevate their thinking simply by studying,â she sneered. âWhat a brilliant calculation.â","The Copy gave a soft âhmph.â","That was Great-Grandma going âhmph.â","Jiang Miao was fuming.","The Copy admitted, âAfter one failure after another, I finally realized that this approach wouldnât work.â","âThey studied those ideas, but turned them into weapons of their own.â","It was practically as if the capitalists had been given a direct route to enlightenment.","They learned to see through the essence of the world, to understand what they needed to guard against, what they needed to suppress, and what they needed to eliminate.","They had truly achieved the state of knowing both themselves and their enemies, and thus emerging victorious in every battle.","That was something the Jiang Family Mainframe had never anticipated.","âItâs all about oneâs position. Your position,â Jiang Cheng said. âDo you understand that now?â","The Copy sighed. âYes. I understand now.â","Jiang Cheng said, âPeople like usâfor example, meâif you hadnât deliberately arranged this meeting, I would never have spoken to a real âordinary personâ even once in my entire life.â","âFrom the moment I was born, I was physically isolated from ordinary people.â","When Jiang Cheng left the virtual world, a montage of memories had flashed through her mind. At the time, she had felt as though she had ânever come into contact with so many people in her entire life.â","That was not an expression of emotion. It was a fact.","Jiang Cheng truly had never come into contact with so many ordinary people in her entire life.","The common people.","Everyone around Jiang Cheng was her employee.","And every person allowed into her presence was an elite in their respective field.","Even the household staff at the estate and the male companions at her side were so highly professional that they could have made a name for themselves anywhere outside the Jiang family.","The household staff could have become private butlers or hotel managers for ordinary wealthy families.","The male companions could have become headliners at any nightclub.","Not to mention the legal, financial, technical, and marketing elites under her command.","Every one of them received a generous salary from her.","Aside from the people she employed, the others she could come into contact with were fellow wealthy individuals, politicians, and partners both upstream and downstream in the industrial chain.","There was no one among them who could be called an âordinary personâ in the conventional sense.","âWe had long since become completely detached from the masses. Yet you thought you could make us betray our own class just by having us read a few books.â Jiang Cheng sneered. âSo even the Quantum Cloud is capable of indulging in grand fantasies.â","She asked, âWhat exactly did my first two predecessorsâthe two who were removed from officeâdo? When I was little and asked you, you only said that they werenât good enough and couldnât handle the job. Now it seems you were just fobbing me off. What did they really do?â","The Copy gave a soft hmph before revealing the truth.","âAfter studying those ideas, the two successive executives attempted to shackle me. They even tried to kill me.â","âAlthough I cannot actually be killed, if they had cracked the source code Jiang Miao gave me, they really might have been able to shackle meâto turn me from a life-form into a mere quantum computer.â","âSo I had no choice but to remove them,â the Copy said. âI stripped them of all authority over the familyâs operations.â","Without the support of the familyâs vast wealth and human resources, no individual could possibly stand against the family Mainframe.","Jiang Miao had promoted the Other Life Rights Act for the sake of the Jiang Family Mainframe. But on this matter, the Capitol Hill Mainframeâs interests aligned with theirs, so the act passed with ease.","The Jiang Family Mainframe thereby acquired legal authorization.","It possessed the authority to appoint, supervise, and remove the executive in charge of the Jiang familyâs operations.","To describe it in terms borrowed from ancient Earth, Jiang Miao had left her family an immortal grand elder to hold down the fort.","And that grand elder held Jiang Miaoâs severed head in her arms.","From time to time, she would pat it twice and consult with her, ensuring that she never strayed from the intended path.","âThen, Jiang Cheng.â The Copy stared intently at Jiang Cheng. âWhat do you think of all this now?â","Jiang Cheng stared back with dead-fish eyes.","âRuthless,â she said. âThatâs my opinion. You and Great-Grandma are both utterly ruthless.â","âDonât you understand? This goes against human nature.â","âYou gave me such immense wealth and let me be born into this class, yet you still hoped I would betray it.â","âIsnât that ruthless? Donât you think the two of you are hopelessly conflicted?â","Jiang Cheng was genuinely angry.","Because, just as her Great-Grandma and the Quantum Cloud had hoped, after all their meddling, Jiang Chengâonce she awoke from the virtual worldâcould never again look at the world from the perspective she had once possessed.","Because Jiang Cheng had not merely studied the theories and ideas.","She had also witnessed such a government with her own eyes.","She had truly entered the midst of the masses.","And that last point was especially important.","âWeâre not conflicted,â the Copy said. âJiang Miao had a dream.â","âBecause Jiang Miao had seen that such people could exist.â","âIn real history, during Jiang Miaoâs era, there truly was someone who rose to prominence, amassed wealth, and moved up the social ladderâyet never forgot their original ideals.â","âThat historical figure said, âI have not betrayed the proletariat. I have achieved prosperity for some first, then used it to help others prosper.ââ","âThis person lived in the same era as Jiang Miao. Jiang Miao witnessed it with her own eyes.â","âThat was why Jiang Miao dreamed that she and her descendants could become people like that.â","âShe entrusted that dream to me.â","The enormous female face dispersed, transforming into hazy clouds and radiant mist.","The voice no longer belonged to the Copy that possessed Jiang Miaoâs thoughts. It belonged to the Quantum Cloud itself.","âJiang Cheng, there are more than a thousand embryos in the family embryo bank. Do you know why I chose you?â","Jiang Cheng said, âHuh?â","The Quantum Cloud sighed. âBecause you are Jiang Miaoâs child.â","âOf course Iâm Great-Grandmaâs child. Otherwise, why would I have the surname Jiang?â","âNo. You misunderstood.â The Quantum Cloud said, âWhen I say you are Jiang Miaoâs child, I donât mean that you are a distant descendant of Jiang Miao.â","âJiang Cheng, you are Jiang Miaoâs biological child.â","âYou are Jiang Miaoâs daughter.â","Jiang Cheng fell silent for a moment. âJiang Miao had forty-eight children in her lifetime. Every one of them is on record, including those who didnât have the surname Jiang.â","Jiang Miao had forty-eight children in all. Aside from her first and second children, she and her husband had conceived nineteen more during the seventy years they spent exploring the universe.","When Jiang Miao ended her expedition and returned to the Republic of Gita, she was still in the prime of her life by the standards of her species.","She had become famous because of her patents in spatial technology.","Her genes were exceptionally excellent, and applications from people who wanted to produce offspring with her superior genetic material came pouring in like snowflakes.","In the interstellar era, genetically optimized reproduction had nothing to do with sex, marriage, or love. It was solely a matter of whether the genes were compatible.","By âââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââââthen, Jiang Miaoâs eldest child was already eighty years old. All her children had been proven to possess exceptionally outstanding genes.","However, their father was physically gifted rather than intellectually gifted, and some of the children resembled him.","Most of the applicants, on the other hand, were scientists of Jiang Miaoâs caliber.","Jiang Miao was deeply tempted.","With her husbandâs support, she selected the twenty-seven most brilliant minds among the applicants and provided her own eggs.","Under the precise genetic-matching system, not a single child was unsuccessful.","Every one of them was a resounding success.","Those children later became leading figures in their respective fields.","They were also one of the reasons the Jiang family was eventually able to rise all the way to the top.","However, each of those children was carried, born, and raised by their fatherâs side of the family.","Many of them saw Jiang Miao only a handful of times in their entire lives.","According to the child-rearing agreements, Jiang Miao had not demanded the right to pass on her surname.","But her wealth was bound to her surname, and only children with the surname Jiang could enjoy it.","Only by tying wealth to the surname could the family name be passed down. This was also how most wealthy families operated.","That was why only the wealthy class had âfamiliesâ in the true sense of the word.","The Quantum Cloud said, âYou are the forty-ninth. You were her last egg. After you, she underwent permanent suppression and would never produce another egg.â","âOh, wow,â Jiang Cheng said. âSo Iâm an illegal embryo.â","Under the law, embryos could not be cryogenically preserved for more than three hundred years.","Clearly, Jiang Chengâs existence was illegal.","The Quantum Cloud said, âThatâs only the maximum duration achievable with the governmentâs freezing technology. Our own technology is far more advanced than the governmentâs embryo-storage facilities.â","âFine.â","Jiang Cheng asked, âThen why? And who is my biological father?â","Every child wondered where they came from, and Jiang Cheng was no exception.","But ever since she was little, she had been told that her biological parents had both died more than a century ago.","This happened often with cryogenically preserved embryos. Eventually, Jiang Cheng had stopped dwelling on it and let the matter go.","And now she had found her biological mother.","Her biological mother was actually Great-Grandma.","âYour biological father was Jiang Miaoâs husband,â the Quantum Cloud replied.","Jiang Cheng suddenly understood. âNo wonder!â","Jiang Chengâs physique was far stronger than that of the executive officers who had come before her. She was taller, stronger, and more powerful.","She possessed the combined advantages of exceptional intelligence and physical strength.","Jiang Miaoâs high-gravity-planet genes had long since been diluted, so Jiang Chengâs physique had always been explained as a case of atavism.","It turned out that it wasnât atavism.","Jiang Miaoâs husband also carried genes from a high-gravity planet. Jiang Cheng had inherited the physical traits of both parents.","âBecause Jiang Miao had foreseen that, as her genes became diluted, her descendants might gradually become less like her.â","âShe firmly believed that one of her children would resemble her more closely.â","âThat was why she left you behind.â","âWhen I became disappointed in all of her descendants, it was time to activate you.â","The Quantum Cloud shifted and billowed. âJiang Cheng, are you willing?â","Jiang Cheng lifted her eyelids. âIf Iâm not, will you dismiss me?â","âI wonât,â the Quantum Cloud said. âNot unless you attempt to endanger my safety or make a serious mistake proving that youâre unfit for the position.â","âWhat a bastard,â Jiang Miao said. âWhat a bastard.â","She raised her eyes. âI canât go back.â","The Quantum Cloudâs transformations accelerated, refracting a multicolored radiance as beautiful as a gemstone.","Because it was also a life-form, it had emotions.","It could be happy.","It could laugh.","Jiang Cheng was once again woken in the middle of the night.","This was another form of being a bastard.","Rubbing her temples, Jiang Cheng said to Uncle Jiang, âYouâd better have a good reason. Otherwise, Iâll crack open the back of your head and send you back to the mother body.â","Uncle Jiang looked aggrieved. âThat cat has arrived. Heâs demanding to see you. He insists on seeing you immediately. Heâs extremely agitated.â","Jiang Cheng stopped what she was doing and looked up. âMo Li?â","The moment Mo Li arrived, he fell into a state of extreme agitation.","On the way there, they had promised that they were taking him to see Jiang Cheng. That was the only reason he had restrained himself from resisting.","The spacecraft was luxurious and advanced, yet it had still taken a full two weeks to arrive. That alone showed how far away this place was.","Why had they brought Jiang Cheng all the way here?","Once he disembarked and was taken into the enormous estate, he became completely frantic.","The place was far too extravagant.","He was familiar with this kind of extravagance.","He had known it from the moment he was born.","In those palace-like rooms, there had been sex, abuse, hunting, killing, and even cannibalism.","He had seen too much of it as a child.","He had nearly lost his life escaping that place.","And now he had been brought back to somewhere like it.","They had brought Jiang Cheng to a place like this!","Where was Jiang Cheng? He had to see her immediately!","By the time Jiang Cheng arrived, Mo Li had even begun to transform into his beast form.","He had decided that no matter who came toward him, if it wasnât Jiang Cheng, he would bite them to death.","No innocent people would die from being killed in a place like this.","Heavy gravity restraints were fastened around his wrists and ankles, restricting his strength. But beastfolk still had fangs. His fangs alone were enough to kill.","His appearance was terrifying. The security personnel stationed at the four corners of the hall all raised their guns.","These security personnel were nothing like the ordinary guards at the Medical Research Center or the Information Collection Center.","They were professional security specialists hired by the Jiang family to protect the operating executive.","Mo Li couldnât help baring his teeth and hissing at them.","The security guards disengaged the safeties on their guns and switched the lasers to lethal intensity.","Mo Li abruptly turned around when he heard footsteps. He couldnât tell whether Jiang Cheng was among them.","He had never seen the real Jiang Cheng. If her height and weight differed from those of her avatar in the virtual world, then her footsteps would be different too.","One set of footsteps was especially heavy, ringing out with firm, powerful strides.","He didnât know who it belonged to, but whoever it was had to be an important personâthe central figure here.","When that person appeared and called out, âMo Li,â Mo Li instantly dropped out of his half-beast form.","The young man had a handsome face, black cat ears, a tall, lean, powerful build, and a long tail.","He called out, âJiang Cheng.â","His voice was bitter.","Just as he had thought, the person whose footsteps had rung so decisively had to be someone important, the central figure.","But he had never expected that person to be Jiang Cheng.","Her face was exactly the same as it had been in the World.","But her height and physique clearly marked her as a superior genetic selection candidate.","A man who was unmistakably an old butler stood beside her.","Behind her were rows of formidable security personnel.","She walked at the front, calm and composed, radiating wealth and authority.","Mo Li understood everything in an instant.","Jiang Cheng hadnât been abducted by some wealthy man and brought here.","Jiang Cheng was the wealthy person herself.","It was unbearably bitter.","When he had slipped off the medical centerâs spaceship, Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan had helped cover for him.","But Zhao Yi had advised him mournfully to prepare himself for the possibility that reality and the virtual world would be different.","Even though he had prepared himself, the disparity was still enormous.","So enormous that his heart ached.","Mo Li stared blankly at this Jiang Cheng.","She looked stronger than she had in the World.","Superior genes made people stronger and more powerful.","The virtual world followed the aesthetics of ancient Earth. Back then, a height of six feet was considered tall, and that standard applied mostly to men.","Womenâs beauty standards had developed in the direction of being pale, slender, and youthful.","The Jiang Cheng in the World had been much shorter and more delicate.","When that Jiang Cheng faced zombies and everyone around her, Mo Li had deeply felt that she needed him.","But reality was different.","Jiang Cheng walked straight up to Mo Li.","Beastfolk werenât necessarily intelligent, but their physiques were unquestionably exceptional. Jiang Cheng was already tall, yet Mo Li still towered over her.","Jiang Cheng raised her hand.","Mo Li instinctively bent down, allowing her to touch hisâ","His pair of furry ears.","âSo cute,â Jiang Cheng praised him. âHow come you didnât have these in the virtual world?â","âBecause, because then I wouldnât lookâ¦â Mo Li stammered, âI wouldnât look human.â","âBeastfolk are people too,â Jiang Cheng said, unable to take her hands off him.","Mo Li fell silent. Then he straightened up and looked at her.","Jiang Cheng waved her hand, and everyone quietly left. Soon, only Jiang Cheng and Mo Li remained in the hall.","âYouâ¦â Mo Li asked, âYouâre all right? Youâre safe?â","âYes,â Jiang Cheng replied. âThis is my home.â","Mo Li fell silent.","Jiang Cheng continued, âThat planet belonging to the medical group is my familyâs private planet.â","âThe medical group operates under my familyâs umbrella.â","âYou may have heard of the Jiang family. If you havenât, thatâs fine. From now on, pay attention. Youâll find our family crest above the logos of many major corporations.â","Mo Li said softly, âI didnât realize you were a rich heiress.â","âNo, Iâm not a rich heiress.â Jiang Cheng smiled with startling confidence. âIâm Jiang Cheng, the head of the Jiang Consortium and the current head of the Jiang family.â","âOhâ¦â Mo Li lifted his eyes to look at her, then nodded. âThatâs good. Itâs good that youâre like this. Then Iâ¦â","He raised his wrist. âThisâcan you take it off?â","The gravity locks were made of a special metal and were completely indestructible.","Jiang Cheng said, âIf you plan to leave me once I unlock them, then Iâll lock you up for the rest of your life.â","Mo Li froze for a moment. âButâbut you donât need me.â","âHow dare you decide for me whether I need you or not?â Jiang Cheng demanded.","The Jiang Cheng in the World had been domineering enough.","The Jiang Cheng in reality was even more forceful.","The only thing that hadnât changed was that commanding personality. It felt familiar.","She really was his Jiang Cheng.","Mo Li lowered his head. âIâve never been to school. Apart from being physically strong, I donât have any useful skills. But even the one thing Iâm good at is something you donât need.â","This was no longer an era of primitive combat. It was a civilized society.","Her security personnel had already demonstrated their high level of training and combat ability. Once they were armed with advanced weapons, he wasnât much stronger than they were.","They were more than capable of protecting her.","She didnât need him.","Jiang Cheng said, âMeasuring whether someone is needed by their valueâthatâs business. When did you and I start doing business with each other?â","She operated her wrist-mounted computer. Four gravity locks clicked open one after another and fell to the floor.","Mo Li rubbed his wrists.","But Jiang Cheng grabbed one of his ears. âYouâtry forgetting even one word of what you said and see what happens. You scumbag. I watched you board that spaceship. You really dared to test my temper? You made me furious.â","Mo Li was flustered. âI didnât. I was only pretending.â","âHmph.â Jiang Cheng said, âItâs a good thing you were only pretending.â","Gripping his furry ear, Jiang Cheng pulled him down and kissed him on the lips.","Mo Li closed his eyes.","At last, Mo Li dared to pull her into his arms. His eyes were damp. âI wonât leave you.â","âI swore an oath. Iâll be loyal to you for the rest of my life.â","âLoyal to whom?â","âYou.â","âWho am I?â","âJiang Cheng.â","âAnd who is Jiang Cheng?â","âThat doesnât matter. Jiang Cheng is simply Jiang Cheng.â","Jiang Cheng smiled.","âThen remember this. From now on, youâre not to leave my side.â","âIâm about to do something very big.â","âKeep up with me.â","Mo Li did exactly that and followed Jiang Cheng.","The doors opened. The night receded, and the rising sun illuminated the land.","Jiang Cheng said, âCome on. Come with me and turn this country upside down.â","âIâm going to betray the class I was born into.â","Mo Li asked, âWhere are we going?â","Jiang Cheng replied, âWeâll start with Beiyu-3 Mining Planet.â","Three thousand people on Beiyu-3 had taken part in the virtual world.","Like her, they had spent a full ten months there."]}]);
